---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'USIVA Field Notes | Questions Before the Form';
const description = 'USIVA field notes turn visa-readiness and compliance questions into careful reading paths, source checks, and practical next actions.';
const canonical = 'https://usiva.org/blog.html';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  activePath="/blog.html"
  canonical={canonical}
  topbarMessage="Field notes are orientation · verify the current source before acting."
  topbarLink={{ label: 'Open official tools', href: '/official-tools.html' }}
>
  <section class="notes-intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="shell-container notes-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The USIVA desk</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">The useful immigration question is usually earlier than the form.</h1>
        <p class="notes-intro__lede">These notes help readers slow down at the right moment: before a document is missing, before an activity is assumed to be authorized, and before a general promise gets mistaken for a personal answer.</p>
        <nav class="intro-actions" aria-label="Field note next steps">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="#reading-map">Choose a reading path</a>
          <a class="button button--outline" href="/tips-faq.html">Open quick answers</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
      <aside class="desk-note" aria-labelledby="desk-note-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Reading posture</p>
        <h2 id="desk-note-heading">Read broadly. Decide narrowly.</h2>
        <p>Field notes organize questions and point to the agency, school, sponsor, employer, or counsel that controls the next answer.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section desk-intro" aria-labelledby="intro-heading">
    <div class="shell-container desk-intro__grid">
      <p class="folio">EDITORIAL NOTE<br /><span>01</span></p>
      <div class="desk-copy flow">
        <p class="eyebrow">What belongs here</p>
        <h2 id="intro-heading">Planning content with a source trail.</h2>
        <p>USIVA field notes are short ways into questions about documentation, timing, status, work authorization, school coordination, and the point at which individualized advice becomes the responsible next step. Each note keeps its public planning role and source trail visible.</p>
        <p>Read them as orientation. Then verify the current instruction with the school, sponsor, employer, government source, or licensed attorney that controls your situation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--mist" id="reading-map" aria-labelledby="map-heading">
    <div class="shell-container">
      <header class="map-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Reading map</p>
        <h2 id="map-heading">Three ways to enter the desk.</h2>
        <p>Each route ends in a concrete action. The question is more important than the label.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="reading-list">
        <a href="/visa-categories.html"><span>01</span><strong>Before you apply</strong><p>What records, dates, funding questions, and prior history should be organized before the application cycle becomes urgent?</p><em>Review visa categories →</em></a>
        <a href="/employers.html"><span>02</span><strong>When work enters the picture</strong><p>How should a reader distinguish study, assistantship, research exposure, training, travel, and employment before beginning an activity?</p><em>Open employer resources →</em></a>
        <a href="/contacts.html"><span>03</span><strong>When the facts are personal</strong><p>Which details make a general page insufficient, and which authority should receive the question next?</p><em>Prepare a careful handoff →</em></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dispatches" aria-labelledby="dispatch-heading">
    <div class="shell-container dispatches__grid">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Desk index</p>
        <h2 id="dispatch-heading">Questions worth carrying forward.</h2>
        <p>Use these as prompts for your own file. Each note stays anchored to its stage, source, and question.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/other-pages.html">See every route in the atlas <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </header>
      <ul class="dispatch-list">
        <li><a href="/services.html"><span>01</span><div><strong>What is the next decision?</strong><p>Turn a broad immigration worry into a named question with an owner and a date.</p></div><em>Services</em></a></li>
        <li><a href="/tips-faq.html#readiness"><span>02</span><div><strong>What belongs in a readiness packet?</strong><p>Separate identity, academic, funding, travel, and authorization records before they blur together.</p></div><em>FAQ</em></a></li>
        <li><a href="/official-tools.html"><span>03</span><div><strong>What source should I check?</strong><p>Follow the trail from a public rule to the school, sponsor, employer, or agency instruction that applies.</p></div><em>Sources</em></a></li>
        <li><a href="/pricing.html"><span>04</span><div><strong>What am I being asked to pay for?</strong><p>Ask for the provider, deliverable, terms, and limits before confusing a fee with a result.</p></div><em>Scope</em></a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section source-protocol" aria-labelledby="protocol-heading">
    <div class="shell-container protocol-grid">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">The source protocol</p>
          <h2 id="protocol-heading">Use a public source to begin, then confirm with the responsible authority.</h2>
      </header>
      <ol>
        <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Find the primary source.</strong><p>Government pages, school instructions, employer guidance, and sponsor materials may be more current than a summary.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Check the date and fit.</strong><p>A rule for one status, program, location, or activity serves its defined scope; compare the source to your facts.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Escalate the personal facts.</strong><p>General content points to the responsible authority for a prior refusal, status concern, or individualized legal question.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section notes-next" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
    <div class="shell-container">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Keep reading with intent</p>
        <h2 id="next-heading">Bring one question to the next page.</h2>
        <p>Continue to a longer article, a short research brief, or the official source directory when you are ready to verify.</p>
      </header>
      <ul class="next-links">
        <li><a href="/articles.html"><strong>Articles</strong><span>Longer explanations with explicit limits.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/briefs.html"><strong>Research briefs</strong><span>Short source-led notes for a defined planning question.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/official-tools.html"><strong>Official tools</strong><span>Direct handoffs to government and program resources.</span></a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .notes-intro {
    background: var(--color-paper);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .notes-intro__grid {
    align-items: end;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 0.7fr);
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .notes-intro h1 {
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .notes-intro__lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
    max-width: 59ch;
  }

  .intro-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .desk-note {
    border-block: 3px solid var(--color-gold);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .desk-note h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    max-width: 19ch;
  }

  .desk-note p:last-child {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .desk-intro__grid,
  .dispatches__grid,
  .protocol-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.3fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  }

  .desk-copy {
    max-width: 64ch;
  }

  .desk-copy h2,
  .map-heading h2,
  .dispatches h2,
  .protocol-grid h2,
  .notes-next h2 {
    max-width: 25ch;
  }

  .folio {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .folio span {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block-start: 0.35rem;
  }

  .map-heading {
    max-width: 56rem;
  }

  .reading-list,
  .dispatch-list,
  .protocol-grid > ol,
  .next-links {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line-dark);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .reading-list {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .reading-list a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem 1.2rem;
    grid-template-columns: 2.2rem minmax(13rem, 0.55fr) minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .reading-list a + a,
  .dispatch-list li,
  .protocol-grid > ol li,
  .next-links li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .reading-list a > span,
  .dispatch-list a > span,
  .protocol-grid > ol li > span {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .reading-list strong,
  .dispatch-list strong,
  .next-links strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .reading-list p,
  .dispatch-list p,
  .next-links span {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .reading-list em,
  .dispatch-list em {
    color: var(--color-accent-dark);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 750;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .dispatches {
    background: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .dispatches__grid {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.72fr) minmax(0, 1.28fr);
  }

  .dispatches__grid > header {
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .text-link {
    color: var(--color-accent-dark);
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    font-weight: 750;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-1);
  }

  .dispatch-list a {
    align-items: start;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    grid-template-columns: 2.2rem minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .dispatch-list strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block-end: 0.2rem;
  }

  .source-protocol {
    background: var(--color-navy);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .source-protocol h2 {
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .protocol-grid > ol li {
    color: var(--color-on-dark-muted);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    grid-template-columns: 2.2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .protocol-grid > ol li strong {
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .protocol-grid > ol li p {
    color: var(--color-on-dark-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
  }

  .protocol-grid > ol li > span {
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .notes-next {
    background: var(--color-mist);
  }

  .notes-next > div > header {
    max-width: 58rem;
  }

  .next-links {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .next-links li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .next-links a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem 1.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 0.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .notes-intro__grid,
    .desk-intro__grid,
    .dispatches__grid,
    .protocol-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .reading-list a {
      grid-template-columns: 2.2rem minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    }

    .reading-list p {
      grid-column: 2 / -1;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .intro-actions .button {
      width: 100%;
    }

    .reading-list a,
    .dispatch-list a,
    .next-links a {
      grid-template-columns: 2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    }

    .reading-list p,
    .reading-list em,
    .dispatch-list em {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }
</style>
